truth or demonstration images.\nManipulation guidance: after visually aligning, close at a stationary pose and allow settling. A nonzero finger gap on the table is contact evidence, not proof of a secure grasp. Test each grasp by lifting only 0.01 m first, using motion_steps=16 or more, then hold 8..16 steps and request the active wrist plus overlook views. Keep orientation and base fixed during this test. Check both finger gap and RGB to confirm the object rises with the gripper before further lifting or transport. If it remains on the table or slips, lower and adjust local contact depth/centering using current images. There is no fixed limit on failed grasp attempts; retry or change approach within the remaining experiment budgets. Avoid large instantaneous target jumps while holding an object; use motion_steps for controlled transport. Total steps per waypoint must remain <=64 and includes the ramp. Use only the active wrist for local corrections, adding overlook when establishing alignment, testing grasp, or verifying placement.\nRGB inputs are downsampled: overlook 640x360, wrist 384x288; no crop or object annotation.\nThe saved ICL demonstration remains available through query_icl throughout this episode. Revisit it when the target region, stage order or arm roles are unclear, and when repeated failures or a change of approach make the reference useful. Use view=text for the original annotation and keyframe index, view=frames with frame_indices for selected images, or view=all for the full reference. Indices are zero-based entries in the keyframe index, not source video frame numbers. Querying does not advance simulation. Ground actions in the current RGB/state.",
